            "body": "> It’s a duplicate of the test below.\r\n> \r\n> https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/blob/main/tests/models/language/pooling_mteb_test/test_qwen3_reranker.py\r\n> \r\n> Please try to minimize the number of tests added to tests/entrypoints/pooling/, particularly model-specific ones. Since they are triggered by almost every PR, they take up too much CI resources.\r\n> \r\n> In contrast, tests in tests/models/language/ only run during daily CI, so they’re more suitable for model-specific tests.\r\n\r\nThanks, this makes sense. This is not identical to the existing MTEB/model test because my intent was to cover the online `/score` and `/rerank` path with `--chat-template`, which was the path discussed in #39784. But I agree it overlaps with the existing Qwen3 reranker model coverage and adds a model-specific server test under `tests/entrypoints/pooling/` which may negatively impact CI resources.\r\n\r\nI can close this PR, or rework the coverage into a non-entrypoints location if you think an online-path regression is still worth preserving elsewhere.",
